.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt NODE-UPDATE.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm node-update.sh
.Nd verify and install a MANET tools update
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -routine
.Op Fl -development
.Op Fl -allow-downgrade
.Op Fl -recover-only | Fl -recover-files | Fl -cancel-kernel-trial
.Nm
.Fl -local-archive Ar path
.Fl -local-version Ar version
.Op Fl -allow-downgrade
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
selects the stable GitHub release marked Latest and installs the board's
tools archive if its version is newer.
Run it as root.
Downloads require qualified clock synchronization, recorded in
.Pa /run/initial_time_synced .
Without that marker, the command reports that the clock is not synced.
Local archive recovery does not require clock synchronization.
The archive digest, paths and embedded versions are checked before staging.
The tools archive may carry any component selected for the release,
including kernels, modules, firmware and configuration migrations.
Current packages update runtime files and managed radio firmware.
CM4 kernel payloads start a one-shot trial by default using a profile derived
from the node's boot files and hardware.
Set enabled=n in
.Pa /etc/manet-kernel-update.conf
to install runtime files only.
An already armed trial still resolves before another update.
Confirmation checks local services, watchdog, mounts, modules and attached
radio PHYs without requiring Ethernet, peers, internet or clock synchronization.
A local bench profile remains an override.
Rock 3A kernel activation is not yet enabled.
Follow the selected release's activation and reboot instructions.
.Pp
A pending installation resumes from its saved archive before checking
for a new release.
Individual files are replaced atomically, but the whole update has no
automatic rollback.
Errors are logged under the journal identifier
.Li manet-update .
.Pp
With
.Li auto_update=y
in
.Pa /etc/mesh.conf ,
automatic stable checks are queued after direct-uplink readiness, acquisition
of a mesh-gateway default route, initial clock synchronization, and daily.
The daily timer adds up to two hours of random delay and catches missed
calendar events after downtime.
Every check requires a direct uplink default route or a next-hop default on
.Li br0 ,
plus the clock marker.
Mesh checks wait a random 0 to 900 seconds before invoking the updater;
direct-uplink checks do not add that delay.
Route refreshes and gateway switches do not queue extra checks.
All automatic checks retain the routine 24-hour throttle.
Disabling automatic updates makes these triggers exit without checking.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -routine
Suppress console output and skip release checks for 24 hours after a
successful check or installation.
Pending recovery bypasses this delay.
.It Fl -development
Select the most recently published build, including prereleases,
for this invocation.
.It Fl -allow-downgrade
Allow the selected release to replace a newer installed version.
.It Fl -recover-only
Finish a pending update from local recovery files without networking.
Do nothing if no update is pending.
.It Fl -local-archive Ar path Fl -local-version Ar version
Install an explicitly supplied board tools archive with its adjacent SHA-256
sidecar and the specified embedded version, without release discovery.
An equal installed version is reinstalled. Downgrades still require
.Fl -allow-downgrade .
.It Fl -cancel-kernel-trial
Cancel an uncommitted kernel trial after returning to the original kernel.
Retain candidate files and diagnostics.
.It Fl -recover-files
Restore a pending payload before service startup, leaving final service
checks and completion to the later recovery pass.
Do nothing if no update is pending.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl -recover-only .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/manet_version.txt , /usr/local/bin/version.txt
Installed version markers.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-update/
Staging and saved recovery data; an
.Pa in-progress
marker records unfinished installation.
.It Pa /run/manet-update.lock
Lock excluding concurrent updates.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after an update or recovery succeeds, or when no work is needed,
including when another updater holds the lock.
Exits 1 on an operating error and 2 for invalid arguments.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Select the newest published build:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo node-update.sh --development
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr journalctl 1 ,
.Xr manet-provision-status.sh 8
